      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Idiopathic hypereosinophilic syndrome (IHES) is characterized by sustained (> 6 months) peripheral eosinophilia (> 1500 cells/mm3), organ damage, and exclusion of other causes. IHES is clinically and pathogenetically heterogenous, and several potential disease mechanisms have been described. The prognosis for patients with IHES has improved with targeted therapies and aggressive management of complications. We report a case of IHES and review the clinical features, evaluation, and options for treatment."},
